					<!-- INTRO / PHILOSOPHY -->
					<section id="philosophy" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">VII. Crafting, Economy & Fallout</h2>
						<blockquote class="quote">"The wild provides. But it never gives anything for free."</blockquote>

						<p class="intro-text">
							Crafting and economy in Untamed are not spreadsheets — they're expressions of the hunt. A hunter's gear is a biography: every cut, scrape, and trophy carries a story. Likewise, the world reacts to what players harvest, kill, trade, or ignore. This chapter gives GMs the tools to run crafting, material rarity, NPC economies, and the ecological fallout that ties everything together.
						</p>

						<h3 class="subsection-title">🛠️ Crafting & Equipment</h3>
						<blockquote class="quote">Gear is born from monsters. Every fang and hide is a puzzle piece — its nature tells you what it wants to become.</blockquote>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Crafting Philosophy</h4>
							<p>Crafting should always feel like:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>The reward for a dangerous hunt</li>
								<li>A collaboration between hunter + material</li>
								<li>A reflection of the biome's identity</li>
							</ul>
							<p>If the hunters kill a thunder-beast, their gear should crackle with spent stormlight. If they slay a swamp horror, their armor should reek of damp rot and stubborn survival.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Crafting Stations</h4>
							<p>Found in:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Hunter lodges</li>
								<li>Villages</li>
								<li>Traveling caravans</li>
								<li>Rare "forge shrines" in deep biomes</li>
							</ul>
							<p>Remote crafting is possible but risky — poor tools increase failure chances, which is a lovely dramatic lever for GMs.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">🔍 Material Tags</h4>
							<p>Every monster part carries tags — mechanical descriptors that shape what it becomes. Tags turn arbitrary loot into intuitive, diegetic design.</p>

							<div class="callout">
								<strong>Examples:</strong>
								<ul>
									<li>lightweight → good for mobility gear</li>
									<li>volatile → bomb cores</li>
									<li>earthbound → armor reinforcement</li>
									<li>conductive → elementally attuned weapons</li>
									<li>regenerative → healing salves</li>
								</ul>
							</div>

							<p>Players don't need a full codex — half the fun is discovering what a strange gland or bone wants to be.</p>
							<p>Crafting must feel like hunting → forging → identity. No spreadsheets. No MMO loot tables. Just monster essence → gear fantasy → tactical identity.</p>
						</div>

						<h3 class="subsection-title">SECTION VII — Crafting, Forging & the Economy of the Wilds</h3>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">🔎 Crafting Philosophy (Revised)</h4>
							<div class="comparison">
								<div class="comparison-col">
									<h5>Crafting in Untamed is:</h5>
									<ul>
										<li>Identity inheritance</li>
										<li>Monster behavior translated into gear</li>
										<li>Horizontal specialization</li>
										<li>GM-curated outcome</li>
									</ul>
								</div>
								<div class="comparison-col">
									<h5>Crafting is not:</h5>
									<ul>
										<li>A stat ladder</li>
										<li>A tier-scaling system</li>
										<li>A way to stack +1 bonuses repeatedly</li>
									</ul>
								</div>
							</div>
							<p>Gear does not scale upward. It diversifies outward. A Tier 1 set can remain viable forever.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- I. CRAFTING STRUCTURE OVERVIEW -->
					<section id="structure" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">I. Crafting Structure Overview</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Every crafted item is built from:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Base Item Type (Weapon or Armor)</li>
								<li>Material Type (Universal table)</li>
								<li>Monster Part Effect (Common drop table)</li>
								<li>Rare Effect (Only if a rare part is used)</li>
								<li>Optional Signature Set (Rare-only, predefined)</li>
							</ul>

							<p>The GM selects appropriate effects based on:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>The monster's identity</li>
								<li>The materials used</li>
								<li>Narrative logic</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Players do not shop menus.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- II. MATERIAL TABLE -->
					<section id="material-table" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">II. MATERIAL TABLE (Universal)</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Material determines playstyle bias, not raw math bonuses.</p>
							<p>Remove:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>+1 attack</li>
								<li>+1 damage</li>
								<li>+1 AR from materials</li>
							</ul>
							<p>Replace with:</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Weapon Materials</h4>

							<div class="table-wrapper">
								<table>
									<thead>
										<tr>
											<th>Material</th>
											<th>Identity</th>
											<th>Effect Pool</th>
										</tr>
									</thead>
									<tbody>
										<tr>
											<td>Metal (Forged / Refined)</td>
											<td>Precise, structured, disciplined.</td>
											<td>Grants access to Control / Support effect pool. Enables structured arrow/song/ability variants.</td>
										</tr>
										<tr>
											<td>Bone / Hide (Predatory / Organic)</td>
											<td>Savage, aggressive, instinctual.</td>
											<td>Grants access to Offensive / Pressure effect pool. Often interacts with Bleed, prone, momentum.</td>
										</tr>
										<tr>
											<td>Stone / Crystal (Resonant / Arcane)</td>
											<td>Volatile, elemental, reactive.</td>
											<td>Grants access to Detonation / Elemental / Utility pool.</td>
										</tr>
									</tbody>
								</table>
							</div>

							<p class="note">("Stone / Crystal" replaces "Stone/Gem" — cleaner and more thematic.)</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Armor Materials</h4>
							<p>Material does not change base AR. Weight determines AR.</p>

							<div class="table-wrapper">
								<table>
									<thead>
										<tr>
											<th>Material</th>
											<th>Effect Pool Access</th>
										</tr>
									</thead>
									<tbody>
										<tr>
											<td>Metal</td>
											<td>Stability / resistance pool access.</td>
										</tr>
										<tr>
											<td>Hide / Bone</td>
											<td>Mobility / aggression pool access.</td>
										</tr>
										<tr>
											<td>Cloth / Membrane</td>
											<td>Positioning / stamina / aura pool access.</td>
										</tr>
									</tbody>
								</table>
							</div>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- III. BASE ARMOR VALUES -->
					<section id="base-armor" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">III. BASE ARMOR VALUES (Locked)</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<div class="table-wrapper">
								<table>
									<thead>
										<tr>
											<th>Weight Class</th>
											<th>Base AR</th>
										</tr>
									</thead>
									<tbody>
										<tr>
											<td>Light</td>
											<td>+2 AR</td>
										</tr>
										<tr>
											<td>Medium</td>
											<td>+3 AR</td>
										</tr>
										<tr>
											<td>Heavy</td>
											<td>+4 AR</td>
										</tr>
									</tbody>
								</table>
							</div>

							<p>Crafting does not increase base AR. Only Signature Sets may modify this, and they replace standard templates.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- IV. WEAPON BASE IDENTITY -->
					<section id="weapon-identity" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">IV. WEAPON BASE IDENTITY (Always Available)</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Certain weapon archetypes are always defined by material:</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Flutes</h4>

							<h5 class="weapon-sub">Bone Flute (Aggressive)</h5>
							<ul>
								<li><strong>Blood Rhythm</strong> — Allies in aura deal +1 melee damage.</li>
								<li><strong>Predator Pulse</strong> — Allies gain +2 to attack rolls.</li>
							</ul>

							<h5 class="weapon-sub">Metal Flute (Defensive)</h5>
							<ul>
								<li><strong>Soothing Tones</strong> — Allies regain HP = CHA mod (min 1) at end of turn.</li>
								<li><strong>Earthen Refrain</strong> — Allies gain +1 AR and advantage vs forced movement.</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Material determines which style of flute is crafted.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Bows</h4>

							<h5 class="weapon-sub">Bone Bow — Offense</h5>
							<ul>
								<li>Piercing Arrows</li>
								<li>Barbed Arrows</li>
							</ul>

							<h5 class="weapon-sub">Metal Bow — Support</h5>
							<ul>
								<li>Signal Arrows</li>
								<li>Binding Arrows</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Material determines arrow package. Not both.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- V. MONSTER EFFECT TABLES -->
					<section id="monster-effects" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">V. MONSTER EFFECT TABLES</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">A. Monster Crafting Output Format</h4>
							<p>Every monster in the Field Guide must define exactly:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>2–3 Common Weapon Effects</li>
								<li>2 Rare Weapon Effects</li>
								<li>2 Common Armor Effects</li>
								<li>1–2 Rare Armor Effects</li>
								<li>1 Signature Craft (Rare Required)</li>
							</ul>
							<p>No monster may exceed these limits. This ensures:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Horizontal diversification</li>
								<li>No effect bloat</li>
								<li>No scaling creep</li>
								<li>Predictable design structure</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">B. Common vs Rare Definition</h4>

							<h5 class="weapon-sub">Common Effects</h5>
							<p>Common effects must:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Be repeatable</li>
								<li>Not introduce new actions</li>
								<li>Not introduce new cooldowns</li>
								<li>Not significantly alter positioning rules</li>
								<li>Not modify base math (no +1 attack, damage, AR, etc.)</li>
							</ul>
							<p>They represent: Minor behavioral inheritance.</p>

							<h5 class="weapon-sub">Rare Effects</h5>
							<p>Rare effects may:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Grant a special action (1/combat or stamina-costed)</li>
								<li>Grant a unique reaction</li>
								<li>Introduce conditional riders</li>
								<li>Interact with terrain</li>
								<li>Modify movement rules</li>
							</ul>
							<p>Rare effects may not:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Grant flat stat bonuses</li>
								<li>Increase base AR</li>
								<li>Increase attack rolls</li>
								<li>Increase damage permanently</li>
								<li>Modify attributes</li>
								<li>Increase stamina regen</li>
							</ul>
							<p>Rare effects represent: Core behavioral inheritance.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">C. Weapon Archetype Translation Rule</h4>
							<p>Monster tables define mechanics. Weapon archetypes define delivery method.</p>

							<p>When applying a selected effect:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Melee Weapons → Direct trigger (on hit / on shove / on movement)</li>
								<li>Bow → Converts effect into special arrow delivery</li>
								<li>Wand → Converts effect into status or spell rider</li>
								<li>Conduit → Converts effect into aspect pulse or terrain modifier</li>
								<li>Flute → Converts effect into aura or rhythm expression</li>
							</ul>

							<p>The mechanical structure does not change. Only delivery flavor changes.</p>

							<div class="callout">
								<strong>Example:</strong> If Rare Effect = "Push 5 ft on hit"
								<ul>
									<li>Bow → Push Arrow</li>
									<li>Wand → Gust Pulse rider</li>
									<li>Conduit → Air Aspect burst</li>
								</ul>
								The effect remains identical in magnitude.
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">D. Material Interaction Rule</h4>
							<p>Material does not create effects. Material filters which effects may be selected.</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Metal → Control / Stability</li>
								<li>Bone/Hide → Momentum / Pressure</li>
								<li>Stone/Crystal → Detonation / Elemental / Utility</li>
								<li>Cloth/Membrane (Armor only) → Positioning / Stamina</li>
							</ul>
							<p>Monster Material Profiles define: How that monster's identity expresses through each bias. They do not contain full abilities. They guide effect tone only.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">E. Effect Cap Rule</h4>
							<p>A crafted weapon or armor may contain:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>1 Common monster effect</li>
								<li>1 Rare monster effect (if rare part used)</li>
							</ul>
							<p>Never more.</p>
							<p>No cross-monster stacking. No dual rare stacking. No multiple common stacking.</p>
							<p>Signature Craft replaces normal template and cannot stack additional rare effects.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- VI. CRAFTING PROCEDURE -->
					<section id="procedure" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">VI. CRAFTING PROCEDURE (GM Flow)</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>When crafting:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Step 1 — Choose Item Type: Weapon or Armor (weight class chosen first)</li>
								<li>Step 2 — Apply Material Identity: This determines which effect pool is accessible.</li>
								<li>Step 3 — Apply Monster Common Effect: GM selects one appropriate Common effect from monster's table.</li>
								<li>Step 4 — If Rare Part Used: GM selects one Rare effect from that monster's Rare table.</li>
							</ul>
							<p>Rare effects never grant flat stat bonuses.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- VII. RARE EFFECT RULE -->
					<section id="rare-effect-rule" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">VII. RARE EFFECT RULE</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<p>Rare effects may grant:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>A special action (1/combat or stamina-costed)</li>
								<li>A reaction</li>
								<li>A conditional rider</li>
								<li>A terrain interaction</li>
								<li>A limited defensive trigger</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Rare effects do NOT grant:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>+1 AR</li>
								<li>+1 attack rolls</li>
								<li>+1 damage</li>
								<li>+1 stamina regen</li>
								<li>+1 power die</li>
								<li>+1 attributes</li>
							</ul>

							<p>No vertical math inflation.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Rare Part Upgrade Rule (Clean Version)</h4>
							<p>A weapon crafted from a monster may be upgraded using that monster's Rare Part.</p>
							<p><strong>Conditions:</strong></p>
							<ul>
								<li>The weapon must already contain that monster's Common effect.</li>
								<li>Only one Rare effect may be added.</li>
								<li>A weapon may only ever contain: 1 Common monster effect, 1 Rare monster effect</li>
								<li>Upgrading replaces nothing — but cannot exceed this cap.</li>
								<li>A weapon cannot contain Rare effects from multiple monsters.</li>
								<li>No cross-monster stacking. No dual-rare stacking.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- VIII. SIGNATURE SETS -->
					<section id="signature-sets" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">VIII. SIGNATURE SETS</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Each monster may define one Signature Set.</p>

							<h4 class="phase-heading">Rules:</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Requires rare part</li>
								<li>Predefined</li>
								<li>Replaces standard armor template</li>
								<li>Cannot stack with additional rare bonuses</li>
								<li>Cannot stack with another signature</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Signature sets may:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Modify AR slightly (+/- 1–2)</li>
								<li>Modify movement</li>
								<li>Grant a unique reaction</li>
								<li>Add a strong identity mechanic</li>
							</ul>

							<p>They are identity anchors, not power upgrades.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- IX. EXAMPLE: WIFFER -->
					<section id="example-wiffer" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">IX. Example — Wiffer (Clean Version)</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Common Weapon Effects</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Melee: On shove, increase knockback by 5 ft.</li>
								<li>Wand: Damage type becomes Blunt.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Rare Weapon Effects</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Bow: Dillo Rush Arrow (DEX save or knockback 5 ft)</li>
								<li>Wand: Detonations apply knockback rider</li>
								<li>Flute: Rolling Song (move 10 ft before attack → gain power die)</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Common Armor Effects</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Advantage vs knockback saves</li>
								<li>Reduce forced movement by 5 ft</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Rare Armor Effect</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Once per combat, ignore forced movement.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Signature Armor — Fierce Dillo Hide (Medium)</h4>
							<p>Replaces standard Medium template.</p>
							<ul>
								<li>+2 AR</li>
								<li>-5 ft movement</li>
								<li>Gain "Curl Block" reaction regardless of weapon.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- TRAP CRAFTING -->
					<section id="trap-crafting" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🧰 7. Trap Crafting (Simple, Flexible, Fiction-Driven)</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p><strong>Required Tools:</strong> Trap Toolkit (reusable)</p>

							<h4 class="phase-heading">Component Formula:</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Component 1 = trigger (meat, sound sac, pheromone gland)</li>
								<li>Component 2 = effect (fire, toxin, shock, spikes)</li>
							</ul>

							<div class="callout">
								<strong>Examples:</strong>
								<ul>
									<li>Meat + Fire Source → Burn Trap</li>
									<li>Vines + Meat → Pitfall Snare</li>
									<li>Vines + Electric Gland → Shock Pitfall</li>
									<li>Clay + Tusk Fragment → Armor Spike Trap</li>
									<li>Resin + Poison Sac → Adhesive Poison Trap</li>
								</ul>
							</div>

							<p>Trap potency = component rarity + placement time.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- POTION & SALVE CRAFTING -->
					<section id="potion-salve" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🧴 8. Potion & Salve Crafting</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Potions (Drinks)</h4>
							<p><strong>Formula =</strong> Herb + Liquid + Tool</p>

							<div class="callout">
								<strong>Examples:</strong>
								<ul>
									<li>Healing Potion → Basic Herb + Clean Water = heal 10 HP</li>
									<li>Super Potion → Herb + Honey/Essence = heal 20 HP</li>
									<li>Stamina Tonic → Root + Monster Part = restore 1d4+CON stamina</li>
									<li>Super Tonic → Root + Resin = restore 1d6 + clear 1 Exhaustion</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">Salves (Applied to Skin)</h4>
							<p><strong>Formula =</strong> Fat/Resin Base + Medicinal Herb/Gland</p>

							<div class="callout">
								<strong>Examples:</strong>
								<ul>
									<li>Healing Salve → regain 5 HP over 3 rounds</li>
									<li>Burn Salve → reduce fire damage or prevent Burn</li>
									<li>Stamina Balm → +1 stamina regen for 3 rounds</li>
									<li>Venom Salve → apply poison resistance or venom coating on weapons</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- IDENTIFYING RECIPES -->
					<section id="identifying-recipes" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🔍 9. Identifying Recipes</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Special sets and weapons require recipe knowledge.</p>

							<p>Hunters learn recipes by:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Asking a crafting vendor</li>
								<li>Bringing materials to a researcher</li>
								<li>Studying monster remains</li>
								<li>Completing village tasks</li>
								<li>Finding lore in ruins</li>
								<li>Dissecting a monster at camp</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Apex and Elder monsters require in-world discovery — a researcher must identify how their parts behave.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- ECONOMY -->
					<section id="economy" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🏘️ 10. Economy & Dynamic Availability</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Crafting relies on:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Barter</li>
								<li>Monster parts</li>
								<li>Favors</li>
								<li>Rare materials</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Prices and materials shift based on:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Monster migration</li>
								<li>Ecology shifts</li>
								<li>Player actions (overhunting, protecting, ignoring)</li>
								<li>Weather disasters</li>
								<li>Village faction politics</li>
							</ul>

							<p>If the players protect caravans → prices drop.</p>
							<p>If they kill a swamp predator → antidotes get cheaper.</p>
							<p>If a Leviathan floods the river → boats become expensive.</p>

							<p>The world is alive. Its economy should be too.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- HARVESTING & RARITY -->
					<section id="harvesting" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🌿 Harvesting & Rarity</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Players should quickly feel which materials are common, rare, or legendary without memorizing tables.</p>

							<h4 class="phase-heading">Rarity Cues:</h4>
							<ul>
								<li><strong>Common:</strong> Hide, bone, basic herbs</li>
								<li><strong>Uncommon:</strong> Glands, tendons, carapace segments</li>
								<li><strong>Rare:</strong> Cores, fangs, essence sacs</li>
								<li><strong>Legendary:</strong> Apex hearts, elder scales, aberrant organs</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Use the story of the monster to determine the value of the parts.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- FALLOUT -->
					<section id="fallout" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">💥 Fallout: The World Responds</h2>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>Every hunt alters the ecosystem — even success carries consequences. This is where Untamed becomes a living-world game instead of a combat simulator.</p>

							<div class="callout">
								<strong>Fallout Examples:</strong>
								<ul>
									<li>Predator slain → prey population surges</li>
									<li>Apex wounded → rival creature moves into territory</li>
									<li>Water serpent killed → algae blooms out of control</li>
									<li>Hive burned → small monsters scatter, altering food chains</li>
									<li>Overhunting → empty sectors, migration, famine</li>
								</ul>
							</div>

							<p>Fallout should guide future hunts, not punish players.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h4 class="phase-heading">GM Tools for Fallout</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Shift monster spawns</li>
								<li>Change shop inventories</li>
								<li>Modify crafting availability</li>
								<li>Trigger biome events</li>
								<li>Unlock new quests or threats</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Players should feel like their victories leave ripples that shape the world.</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- GM SUMMARY -->
					<section id="gm-summary" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🔧 GM Summary</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<p>Crafting tells stories.</p>
							<p>Economy reveals pressure.</p>
							<p>Fallout shapes the next chapter.</p>

							<p>This section is where the world becomes responsive — the connective tissue that makes every hunt part of a larger living ecosystem.</p>
						</div>
					</section>
				</article>
			</div>

			<footer class="footer">
				<div class="container">
					<p>
						This is the Playtest version. Some monster art is AI-generated; the final version will use original artist drawings.
					</p>
					<p class="footer-creed">The wild does not forgive. But it rewards those who respect the hunt.</p>
				</div>
			</footer>
		</main>

		<style>
			* {
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			:root {
				--forest-dark: #1a2e1a;
				--forest-green: #2d5016;
				--moss-green: #4a7c2f;
				--leaf-green: #6b9d3a;
				--amber: #d4a257;
				--earth-brown: #5c4033;
				--cream: #f5f1e8;
				--text-light: #e8e4d8;
			}

			body {
				font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				color: var(--text-light);
				line-height: 1.7;
				min-height: 100vh;
			}

			.container {
				max-width: 1000px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 0 2rem;
			}

			/* Navigation */
			.nav {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
				padding: 1rem 0;
				position: sticky;
				top: 0;
				z-index: 100;
			}

			.nav .container {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: space-between;
				align-items: center;
				max-width: 1200px;
			}

			.logo {
				font-size: 1.5rem;
				font-weight: 900;
				color: var(--amber);
				text-decoration: none;
				letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
			}

			.nav-links {
				display: flex;
				gap: 2rem;
			}

			.nav-links a {
				color: var(--cream);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 500;
				transition: color 0.3s;
			}

			.nav-links a:hover,
			.nav-links a.active {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Breadcrumb */
			.breadcrumb {
				padding: 2rem 0 1rem;
			}

			.breadcrumb a {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 500;
			}

			.breadcrumb a:hover {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Page Header */
			.page-header {
				padding: 2rem 0 2rem;
				text-align: center;
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}

			.page-header h1 {
				font-size: 3rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.subtitle {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				font-style: italic;
			}

			/* TOC */
			.toc {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
				border-radius: 8px;
				padding: 1.75rem 1.75rem 1.25rem;
				margin-bottom: 3rem;
			}

			.toc h2 {
				color: var(--amber);
				font-size: 1.4rem;
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
				text-align: center;
				letter-spacing: 0.05rem;
			}

			.toc-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.5rem;
			}

			.toc-section h3 {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				letter-spacing: 0.08rem;
			}

			.toc-section ul {
				list-style: none;
				padding: 0;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.toc-section li {
				margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
			}

			.toc-section a {
				color: var(--cream);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-size: 0.97rem;
				transition: color 0.2s;
			}

			.toc-section a:hover {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Content */
			.content {
				padding-bottom: 4rem;
			}

			/* Major Sections */
			.major-section {
				margin-bottom: 4rem;
				scroll-margin-top: 100px;
			}

			.section-title {
				font-size: 2.2rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
				padding-bottom: 1rem;
				border-bottom: 3px solid var(--amber);
			}

			.subsection-title {
				font-size: 1.55rem;
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.03rem;
			}

			.intro-text {
				font-size: 1.1rem;
				color: var(--cream);
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
				max-width: 820px;
			}

			/* Rule Sections */
			.rule-section {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				padding: 1.5rem;
				border-radius: 8px;
				margin: 1.5rem 0;
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
			}

			.rule-section.highlight {
				border-color: var(--amber);
				background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--forest-green) 0%, var(--moss-green) 100%);
			}

			.phase-heading {
				color: var(--amber);
				font-size: 1.3rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.03rem;
			}

			.weapon-sub {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				font-size: 1.1rem;
				margin: 1rem 0 0.5rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.02rem;
			}

			.rule-section p {
				color: var(--text-light);
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.rule-section ul,
			.rule-section ol {
				margin-left: 1.5rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.rule-section li {
				margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
				color: var(--text-light);
			}

			.note {
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--moss-green);
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				margin-top: 0.5rem;
			}

			/* Blockquote / Quote */
			blockquote.quote {
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
				padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
				margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
				border-radius: 6px;
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--cream);
				font-size: 1.1rem;
			}

			/* Callout */
			.callout {
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-left: 4px solid var(--leaf-green);
				padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
				margin: 1rem 0;
				border-radius: 6px;
				color: var(--cream);
			}

			.callout strong {
				color: var(--amber);
				display: inline-block;
				margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
			}

			.callout ul {
				margin-left: 1.25rem;
				margin-top: 0.4rem;
			}

			.callout li {
				margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
			}

			/* Comparison (side-by-side lists) */
			.comparison {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
				gap: 1.5rem;
				margin: 1rem 0;
			}

			.comparison-col {
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				padding: 1.25rem;
				border-radius: 6px;
				border: 1px solid var(--earth-brown);
			}

			.comparison-col h5 {
				color: var(--amber);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.03rem;
			}

			.comparison-col ul {
				margin-left: 1.25rem;
			}

			.comparison-col li {
				margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
				color: var(--text-light);
			}

			/* Tables */
			.table-wrapper {
				overflow-x: auto;
				margin: 1rem 0;
				border-radius: 6px;
				border: 1px solid var(--earth-brown);
			}

			.table-wrapper table {
				width: 100%;
				border-collapse: collapse;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				color: var(--text-light);
			}

			.table-wrapper thead {
				background: var(--earth-brown);
			}

			.table-wrapper th {
				text-align: left;
				padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
				color: var(--cream);
				font-weight: 700;
				letter-spacing: 0.04rem;
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
